# Commercial S12.1 final-review diagnosis — trusted environment, snapshot, writer exclusion and JSON types

Date: 2026-09-30

## Finding

The final review of Control `4c87fdcfc0a1b6d629e7f03ccc72cf366ce86edd`
identified four remaining pre-deployment gaps:

1. the immutable staged venv self-hashed bytes copied from a chatops-writable
   source but did not compare them with a reviewed freeze digest;
2. sequential backup reads could form a mixed-generation repository snapshot;
3. a new chatops Git process could explicitly select the fixed quarantined Git
   path after the final process scan; and
4. Python equality allowed integer/boolean and integer/float substitutions in
   an otherwise exact JSON contract.

No merge, release tag or server deployment had begun. The exactly-once runtime
attempt remained unused.

## Root cause

The prior correction made the staged runtime immutable after copy but had not
made the source bytes an input to the reviewed freeze. Backup consistency and
repository recovery relied on repeated process snapshots without separately
binding all pre-state fields or revoking the repository owner's directory
authority. Finally, ordinary Python container equality was used as a schema
comparison even though `bool` subclasses `int`.

## Versioned correction

- Bind the complete canonical venv and resolved interpreter SHA-256 values in
  the manifest and annotated freeze inputs. Validate both before copying, after
  copying and immediately before the only service start.
- Record identity, tree, attached/detached state, release tip, managed refs and
  repository path metadata; re-read the complete repository snapshot after
  backup creation and immediately before the durable attempt marker. Active
  Git or sync activity and any value mismatch are fail-closed.
- While the atomic Git barrier is installed, lock each checkout root against
  chatops traversal/write, make the quarantined Git directory root-only and run
  only the bounded recovery Git commands as root. Restore the recorded
  ownership/modes before reopening the checkout.
- Compare every JSON node recursively with exact Python types before value
  equality. Boolean/integer and integer/float substitutions are rejected.

## Evidence boundary

The environment digests were derived read-only from the canonical Application
venv while Application remained at the reviewed commit/tree. No credential,
identity, provider payload or real-user data was read or retained. The values
are non-secret integrity bindings.

## Rollback

The existing exactly-once backup-first rollback remains authoritative. The
server has not been mutated, so no rollback or second attempt is required at
this stage.
